CC   IMGT/LIGM-DB annotation level: by annotators
CC   
CC   [3] also reports the complete alpha-1 gene and part of the A2m(2)
CC   alpha-2 allele (bases 737-2516; see Sites table). Comparison of the
CC   three sequences suggests that the A2m(1) alpha-2 allele might be a
CC   hybrid of the alpha-1 gene and A2m(2) alpha-2 allele. The hinge
CC   region in the alpha genes occurs at beginning of the CH2 domain.
CC   The alpha-1 hinge region is 13 amino acids longer than that in
CC   alpha-2. Both hinge regions consist of approximate tandem repeats
CC   of a 15 bp sequence. The first repeat occurs 5' to the mRNA splice
CC   site and is non-coding. The authors [3] suggest that this
CC   repetitive structure provides a possible mechanism for the large
CC   number of variations observed in hinge regions. There is a coupled
CC   30 bp insertion, 9 bp deletion in alpha-2 relative to alpha-1
CC   (starting at base 97).
CC   [1] also reports sequences for the epsilon-1 and epsilon-2
CC   (pseudogene) C-region genes. The authors [1] determined the
CC   physical linkage between epsilon-1 and alpha-2 and that between
CC   epsilon-2 and alpha-1. [2] also reports the alpha-1 CH2 domain and
CC   epsilon-2.
CC   This entry is part of a multigene region (region B), which includes
CC   the gamma-2, gamma-4, epsilon-1 and alpha-2 genes. See segment 1
CC   for more comments.
CC   Complete source information:
CC   Human genomic DNA, cosmid Ig10 [1],[3]; placenta DNA [2] clone
CC   H-Ig-alpha-25; genomic DNA from TOU II-5 library clone
CC   lambda-TOU-alpha2 (for A2m(2) allele) [3].
